Description: ACARS decoder (minimal raw-PCM build)
 acarsdec is a multi-channel ACARS (Aircraft Communications Addressing and
 Reporting System) decoder. This package is built for the Web-888 SDR with
 only the libsndfile input enabled: it decodes raw 12 kHz mono S16LE PCM
 from stdin (acarsdec --sndfile file=/dev/stdin,subtype=0x02) and writes
 text reports to stdout. All SDR hardware backends (RTL-SDR, Airspy,
 SDRplay, SoapySDR), ALSA, MQTT and libacars support are disabled.

